Usage & Spend snapshot-backed refresh: `sample` profiles, upstream main vs PR head
================================================================================
Each profile is `/usr/bin/sample <pid> 70` (1 ms interval, so one sample is about 1 ms of thread time)
taken 100 s into the measured window of the run in spend-snapshot-backed-refresh-cpu.log, covering at
least one full 60 s refresh cycle. Counts are samples in which the frame appears on a stack.

1. Samples on the cost-usage dispatch queues (queue labels are readable without symbols)

